# What `gcloud builds submit` uploads for the DASHBOARD BACKEND image.
#
# This directory is submitted as its own source root:
#
#   gcloud builds submit AI-phone-dashboard/backend \
#     --config=cloudbuild.dashboard.yaml --project=vetra-shared-c3a3bd
#
# rather than the repository root, because the root .gcloudignore EXCLUDES
# `AI-phone-dashboard` outright — which is why nothing has ever built this
# image. Un-excluding it there would upload the whole dashboard on every voice
# build for no benefit; submitting this directory keeps both uploads minimal and
# neither build carries the other's source.
#
# THIS FILE MUST EXIST even though it is short. With no .gcloudignore in the
# source root gcloud falls back to .gitignore, which is written for a different
# purpose — that fallback is what let a 278 MiB / 705-file tarball through on
# the voice image's first submit.
#
# Keep in step with .dockerignore. They are not the same list — this one governs
# what leaves the workstation, that one what the daemon sees — but anything
# excluded there and not here is uploaded for no reason.
.git
.gitignore
node_modules
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The test suite. The image does not ship it, and the Dockerfile deletes it
# again on the way in as a belt to this brace.
src/__tests__

*.log
coverage
